course: dictionary
lesson: 1679
title: Chores and everyday words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A chore is a small job you do regularly at home, like washing up, making your bed or feeding the pet. Look at the words around it to see what kind of job it is. «Priya earns extra minutes by doing chores, and her bedroom has never been so tidy.» The tidy bedroom tells you chores are jobs that keep the home in order.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «Doing a chore properly builds trust, and you learn useful skills.» If you put "Doing a job at home properly builds trust", it still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: A chore can also be any boring or unpleasant task, not only a job at home. «People hope robots and AI will help with boring chores, but real home robots are still clumsy and expensive.» The word boring tells you the chores are dull jobs.
fact: A chore is a small job you do regularly, often at home.
fact: «Household chores» are the jobs done around the house, such as tidying, setting the table and putting out the bins.
fact: «A chore chart» shows who does which job.
fact: Some children get pocket money (UK) or an allowance (USA) for doing chores.
fact: «A bit of a chore» means something is a little boring or annoying to do.
exercise: «Priya earns extra minutes by doing chores.» What are chores in this sentence? | Holidays with the family | Days out at the park | Games played on a screen | *Jobs done regularly around the home
exercise: «Money for chores is earned by doing the job well, not by doing it fast and badly.» What does this tell you about chores? | They are only done by grown-ups | They are always fun to do | *They are jobs that can be done well or badly | They are the same as holidays
exercise: What does a chore chart show? | *Who does which job | What the weather will be | How much money you have | Your favourite food
test: «Doing a chore properly builds trust.» What does chore mean here? | A game | *A job or task | A holiday | A type of food
test: Which phrase means something is a little boring to do? | *A bit of a chore | Household game | Chore chart | Pocket money
exam: Which sentence uses chore to mean a boring or unpleasant task? | The children set the table before dinner | *«People hope robots and AI will help with boring chores.» | Sam went to the park | Priya kept her bedroom tidy
